<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tasmola culture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 8th–4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tasmola culture is an early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> archaeological culture of central and northern Kazakhstan, dated to about the eighth to fourth centuries BCE. It is known from burial mounds, some joined to stone ridges known as 'kurgans with moustaches', containing weapons, horse harness and bronze objects in animal style. It is usually counted among the cultures of the Saka world.</p></div>
